    "abstract": [
      {
        "source": "grobid_tei",
        "value": "In the context of fully-homomorphic-encryption, we consider the representation of large integers by their decomposition over a product of rings (through the Chinese Remainder Theorem) and introduce a new algorithm for the determination of the sign solely through the knowledge of ring-components. Our implementation with 128 bits of security delivers a correct result with a probability higher than 1-10-12 in less than 140 ms for 32-bit integers on a laptop."
      },
      {
        "source": "pdfplumber",
        "value": "In the context offully-homomorphic-encryption, we consider the representation of large integers by their decomposition over a product of rings (through theChinese Remainder Theorem) and introduce a new algorithm for the determination of the sign solely through the knowledge of ring-components. Our implementation with 128 bits of security deliv- ers a correct result with a probability higher than 1 − 10−12 in less than 140 ms for 32-bit integers on a laptop."
      },
      {
